=== p2-windows · W7 · page:settings/Helix (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:settings/Helix   kind=page   web route=/integrations/helix
Web source  : web/src/features/settings/pages/HelixPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection +
  registration, unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder)
  and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's idealized "HelixPage.xaml + HelixPageViewModel.cs under
  TeslaSync/Features/Settings" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4
  ShellPageFactory by route name ("Helix"), the route RouteTable already maps (integrations/helix).
- Web HelixPage is a thin <PageContainer title subtitle breadcrumbLabels loading={useSettings().isLoading}>
  wrapping the <AISettings/> component. The native port reproduces that exactly: HelixPage.cs composes the shared
  PageContainer surface (parity port of web/src/components/layout/PageContainer.tsx) with the same three strings +
  the integrations/helix breadcrumb overrides, hosts the already-ported AISettings feature-view as PageContent, and
  binds PageContainer.IsLoading to HelixPageViewModel (the page's own useSettings binding). The AISettings child is
  its own W-prompt surface (feature-views/AISettings) — out of scope here except as the hosted body.
- Data source useSettings (GET /settings) is bound through the shared IAiSettingsSource (the same seam AISettings
  uses); the shell default is the new EmptyAiSettingsSource (mirrors the EmptyXSource convention of the sibling
  BrowserNotificationsPage), which resolves the read to the empty state so the page leaves loading and shows the
  Helix opt-in form. No SI unit-bearing fields on this surface.
- The three i18n keys (helix.page.title, helix.page.subtitle, helix.breadcrumb.integrations) did NOT yet exist in
  the platform catalog; added verbatim (web fallbacks) to Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw in alphabetical
  position (between translation.healthy and translation.help.*). The surface resolves them through the ILocalizer
  facade with the web key names.
- Pre-existing blocker repaired: ShellWindow.xaml.cs (the W4 NavigationView page-factory registration block — an
  allowed file for this prompt) had a malformed "Locations" registration whose lambda was never closed
  (missing `return page; });`), so its body bled into the following "NotificationsArchived" registration. This was
  a hard C# syntax error (CS1026/CS1002/CS1513 at line 255) that failed pass-1 of the WinUI XAML markup compiler and
  cascaded into 84 WMC0001/WMC0110 "unknown type" errors + a WMC9999 internal-compiler crash, i.e. the whole
  TeslaSync.App project (and therefore the solution build, lint and test) was red before any change. The lambda was
  closed to match the sibling Dashboard/Locations registration shape; the build then went green. Repairing a
  pre-existing in-block blocker is the established practice for these page prompts (cf. the ApiLogsPage log's
  Tests.csproj repair).
- TeslaSync.App.Tests references the App surfaces by LINKED Microsoft.UI-free source (not an assembly ref); the two
  Microsoft.UI-free HelixPage sources (HelixPage.Model.cs + HelixPage.ViewModel.cs) were added to its <Compile>
  union in the He* cluster. The Fluent view (HelixPage.cs) is exercised by the app build, as for every sibling page.

=== PARITY ===
PARITY_REQUIRED=5

# Panels (0) / Charts (0) / Maps (0)
#   The web HelixPage declares no GlassPanel/chart/map of its own — it composes PageContainer + the already-ported
#   AISettings surface (its own prompt). There are no anonymous regions in the web source to reproduce here.

# Data states (2) — loading / success (the two states the web page wires via PageContainer loading={useSettings().isLoading})
[x] state  - loading -> HelixPage.ViewModel.cs#HelixPageViewModel.IsLoading (web useSettings().isLoading; field-init true,
             set in #StreamSettingsAsync as `result.Status == LoadStatus.Loading`); bound to the container via
             HelixPage.cs#SyncLoading -> PageContainer.IsLoading, rendered as the PageContainer loading spinner.
             Tests: HelixPageTests.ViewModel_starts_in_the_loading_state, ViewModel_stays_loading_while_only_a_loading_emission_is_seen.
[x] state  - success -> once the settings read resolves (LoadStatus.Loaded/Empty) HelixPageViewModel.IsLoading flips
             false -> HelixPage.cs#SyncLoading clears PageContainer.IsLoading -> the container renders
             PageContent = AISettings (the Helix opt-in form). HelixPage.cs#HelixPage(...) sets PageContent = _settings.
             Tests: HelixPageTests.ViewModel_resolves_out_of_loading_on_a_loaded_settings_document, ViewModel_resolves_out_of_loading_when_settings_arrive.

# Strings (3) — every visible literal resolves from Strings/*.resw via ILocalizer with the web key names
[x] string - helix.breadcrumb.integrations -> HelixPage.Model.cs#HelixPageRegistration.IntegrationsBreadcrumb
             localizer.GetString("helix.breadcrumb.integrations", "Integrations"); folded into #BreadcrumbOverrides
             (integrations segment) and published to PageContainer.breadcrumbOverrides in HelixPage.cs. resw rows:
             translation.helix.breadcrumb.integrations (en/he/ar). Tests: IntegrationsBreadcrumb_resolves_the_web_key_with_the_web_fallback,
             Registration_resolves_every_required_string_key_from_the_catalog, BreadcrumbOverrides_resolve_each_segment_from_the_catalog.
[x] string - helix.page.subtitle -> HelixPage.Model.cs#HelixPageRegistration.Subtitle localizer.GetString(
             "helix.page.subtitle", "Optional AI integration. Off by default — nothing runs until you opt in here.");
             set as PageContainer.Subtitle in HelixPage.cs. resw rows: translation.helix.page.subtitle (en/he/ar).
             Test: HelixPageTests.Subtitle_resolves_the_web_key_with_the_web_fallback.
[x] string - helix.page.title -> HelixPage.Model.cs#HelixPageRegistration.Title localizer.GetString("helix.page.title",
             "Helix"); used as the PageContainer title and the breadcrumb "helix" segment label. resw rows:
             translation.helix.page.title (en/he/ar). Tests: HelixPageTests.Title_resolves_the_web_key_with_the_web_fallback,
             BreadcrumbOverrides_map_the_integrations_and_helix_segments.

PARITY_COVERED=5
